---
import Layout from "@layouts/ComponentsLayout.astro";
import Button from "@components/button/index.astro";
---

<Layout>
  <h1 class="govuk-heading-xl">Button</h1>
  <p class="govuk-body">
    Buttons have been adapted from the GOV.UK Design System to fit the needs of
    i.AI apps. Jump to
    <a href="#deviation" class="govuk-link">the deviation section</a> to see what
    has changed and why.
  </p>
  <h2 class="govuk-heading-m">Default buttons</h2>
  <p class="govuk-body">
    Use the primary button when the action is the main action on the page.
  </p>
  <p class="govuk-body">
    Use the secondary button when the action is a secondary action on the page.
    Where you have multiple buttons on the page, the secondary button has been
    designed to work to be duplicated multiple times
  </p>
  <div class="govuk-button-group">
    <Button variant="primary" href="#">Primary Button</Button>
    <Button variant="secondary" href="#">Secondary Button</Button>
  </div>

  <h2 class="govuk-heading-m">Inverse buttons</h2>
  <p class="govuk-body">
    Use the inverse button when the action is on a dark background.
  </p>
  <div class="inverse-component-container">
    <Button variant="inverse" href="#">Inverse Button</Button>
  </div>
  <h2 class="govuk-heading-m">Link buttons</h2>
  <p class="govuk-body">
    Use the link button to have button functionality but look like a link in
    order to manage the attention given to this item. Be careful to ensure that
    it does not confuse users as to thinking it is a link that goes to another
    section on a page.
  </p>
  <Button variant="link" href="#">Link Button</Button>
  <br />
  <Button variant="link" href="#" underline={false}
    >Link Button with no underline</Button
  >
  <br />
  <br />
  <h2 class="govuk-heading-m">Warning buttons</h2>
  <h4 class="govuk-heading-s">Warning link button</h4>
  <p class="govuk-body">
    Use the delete link button to show a destructive action that can be
    confirmed or cancelled. This is the "quiet" version of the warning button
    below and is designed not to attract attention away from the primary action
    on the page but to show that it is a destructive action at a glance.
  </p>
  <Button variant="warning-link" href="#">Delete</Button>
  <br />
  <br />
  <h4 class="govuk-heading-s">Warning button</h4>
  <p class="govuk-body">
    Use the warning button to confirm a destructive action. This is the "loud"
    version of the delete link button above and is designed to attract the
    attention as the main action.
  </p>
  <Button variant="warning" href="#">Delete</Button>
  <h2 class="govuk-heading-l" id="deviation">
    Deviation from GOV.UK Design System
  </h2>
  <h3 class="govuk-heading-l">Accessibility</h3>
</Layout>
